{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088", "score": 0.107, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-088 | Study family SF-APPS-088: Offensive-identity resilience: connector absence vs usage-matched others\n- observed_research_question: Offensive-identity resilience: connector absence vs usage-matched others\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Connector absence displaces team offensive identity (D_A) more than usage-matched non-organizer absence.\n- observed_result: Unmatched conn vs role D_A 0.2020 vs 0.1021, t=5.97 p=2.87e-08. Usage-matched vs role: paired dD_A +0.1151, P(conn>ctrl)=81.2%, t=6.35 p=7.35e-09 n=96. Vs terminal: +0.0777 t=2.37 p=0.0261 n=25.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Usage-matched connector vs role occupant identity break is large and significant (n=96). Licensed comparison excludes organizers.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=96 matched pairs vs role; n=25 vs terminal; 908 player-seasons\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-014"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-064", "score": 0.101, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-064 | Study family SF-CHT-064: Team-season defensive H2-adjustment reliability\n- observed_research_question: Team-season defensive H2-adjustment reliability\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: A defense's effect on opponents' H2-H1 change is a reliable team trait.\n- observed_result: H2-change trait r=-0.001 (p<.05 needs ~0.18). H1 defensive level r=+0.356 (test works). Season-to-season -0.19, -0.26, +0.16. Offensive H2-change r=+0.139 ns.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_measurement_reliability\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Split-half r=-0.001; a detectable r needs about 0.18.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 120 team-seasons; p<.05 needs r~0.18\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: CHT-064: 'split-half (two halves of a season) correlation across 120 team-season'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-TMP-005"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-078", "score": 0.093, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-078 | Study family SF-APPS-078: Channel 2: possession ending state vs next 90-180s volume/points\n- observed_research_question: Channel 2: possession ending state vs next 90-180s volume/points\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: A possession's ending state changes opponent points/possessions in the next 90-180s beyond ~0.01-0.02 PPP boundary drift.\n- observed_result: 90s vs MADE_DEAD: TURNOVER_LIVE dOppPts=+0.510 dNetPts=-0.306 (dOppPPP=+0.055, dOppPoss=+0.298); MISSED_DEAD dNetPts=-0.112; PUTBACK dNetPts=+0.078. Volume (dOppPoss), not PPP, carries most of the live-TO cost.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- observed_failure_evidence: No inferential tests in the core table; live TO raising opponent possession count is largely definitional (steal starts a break).\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=911968; MADE_DEAD n=354564\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-075\n- observed_verdict: descriptive"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-052", "score": 0.093, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-052 | Study family SF-CHT-052: Play-type replacement similarity vs absorb/cascade\n- observed_research_question: Play-type replacement similarity vs absorb/cascade\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Having a similar-profile teammate separates absorption from cascade when a player sits.\n- observed_result: mean sim ABSORBED +0.863 vs CASCADE +0.848; Spearman(sim, -gap)=-0.19 (wrong-signed). Embiid 23-24 cascades with Reed sim 0.94.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Similarity does not separate absorption from cascade; almost always findable.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPA-005\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-CHT-032\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-CHT-086\n- observed_verdict: null\n- observed_failure_type: B_powered_null"}], "n_results": 4}

